zebkit: views with a window of their own, on macOS.

On Linux the engine gives every view a window and decides where it is: on
the screen when the machine has a display, and nowhere otherwise. WebKit
on macOS leaves the window to the application. zebkit's own source
src/view/ZebkitViewCocoa.mm (zebkit-view.h) does for macOS what the
engine does on Linux; this builds it into WebKit.framework, beside the CDP
endpoint, through the link Source/WebKit/zebkit that
scripts/fetch-upstream.sh makes.

--- a/Source/WebKit/SourcesCocoa.txt
+++ b/Source/WebKit/SourcesCocoa.txt
@@ -951,6 +951,9 @@ zebkit/cdp/CDPTransportCocoa.mm @nonARC
 zebkit/cdp/CDPView.cpp
 zebkit/cdp/CDPViewCocoa.mm @nonARC
 zebkit/cdp/CDPWebSocket.cpp
+
+// zebkit: views with a window of their own (src/view).
+zebkit/view/ZebkitViewCocoa.mm @nonARC
 ModelConnectionToWebProcessMessageReceiver.cpp
 MediaPlayerPrivateRemoteMessageReceiver.cpp @cost:5
 ModelProcessConnectionMessageReceiver.cpp
